HST Office: the lone toolbar beside the window banner takes two even rows (Single toolbar, Sidebar).

Owner decision 14/11/2026 (1.0.2): in the toolbar user interfaces the toolbar block beside the banner is
balanced with it, as in HST PDF: two rows of buttons next to the at least 75 logical px high banner, not one
row centred beside it. The Single toolbar and Sidebar user interfaces (and Draw's Standard one) have a single
docked toolbar, so it breaks into two rows of about equal width.

- vcl: ToolBox::HstSetBalancedLines(2), opt in. While the toolbox is docked horizontally with its menu,
  ImplCalcBreaks breaks once, at the most even place (vcl/inc/HstToolbarRows.hxx, plain arithmetic, unit
  tested): after a separator when the rows then stay within one button of each other (VCL draws no
  separator before a break, so the groups stay whole), otherwise between two buttons; of equally even
  breaks the one with the longer top row. ImplCalcSize reports both rows and ImplFormat no longer stretches
  the one line to the window height. Items keep their size; the rows start at the same left edge. The menu
  (right click: visible buttons, customize, undock, lock, close; clipped items) stays. Floating, vertical
  and all other toolboxes are unchanged. The state lives in vcl's private ImplToolBoxPrivateData, so the ToolBox
  class layout (include/vcl/toolbox.hxx gets two member functions only) stays the same for other modules.
- framework's ToolbarLayoutManager::doLayout opts in only for the one docked toolbar of the top docking area
  when the banner is shown there (hst-banner-always-visible.patch) and both rows fit the banner strip's
  height and the width left of the banner; otherwise, or as soon as another toolbar joins the area, the
  toolbar has one row as before. Docking (drag) and undocking start with the one-row toolbar; the next
  layout gives the two rows back. Nothing is persisted: the docking positions, Visible state, locking and
  customized toolbars in the user profile are those of the one-row toolbar.

Tests: tests/unit/test_toolbar_two_rows.py (break placement), tests/runtime/check-toolbar-two-rows.py
(Writer, Calc, Impress, Draw in their toolbar user interfaces: two rows, even, beside the banner).
